<article class="env-lemma" id="03U9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03U9">Lemma <span data-tag="03U9">64.15.5</span>.</a> Let $P$ be a finite projective $A[G]$-module and $M$ a $\Lambda [G]$-module, finite projective as a $\Lambda $-module. Then $P \otimes _ A M$ is a finite projective $\Lambda [G]$-module, for the structure induced by the diagonal action of $G$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For any $\Lambda [G]$-module $N$ one has 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\Lambda [G]}\left(P \otimes _ A M, N\right)= \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{A[G]}\left(P, \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\Lambda }(M, N)\right)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the $G$-action on $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\Lambda }(M, N)$ is given by $(g\cdot \varphi )(m) = g \varphi (g^{-1} m) $. Now it suffices to observe that the right-hand side is a composition of exact functors, because of the projectivity of $P$ and $M$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>